================================================================================
3. TECHNOLOGY STACK
================================================================================

FRONTEND
- Framework: React 19 (Vite)
- State: AuthContext (Context API)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS (Custom Theme)
- Visuals: Lottie (Animations), FullCalendar (Interactive Scheduling)
- API: Axios with Interceptors

BACKEND
- Framework: Node.js / Express.js
- Database: MongoDB (via Mongoose ODM)
- Auth: JWT (Stateless) + BcryptJS
- Logic: Node-cron (Scheduled accruals), Express Validator (Input Sanitization)
- Mail: Nodemailer

================================================================================
4. FULL API REFERENCE
================================================================================

AUTHENTICATION (/api/auth)
- POST /register: Public registration.
- POST /login: Secure authentication.
- GET /profile: Fetch authenticated user state.
- PUT /profile: Update user specific metadata.

LEAVE OPERATIONS (/api/leaves)
- POST /apply: Submit leave (Logic: Balance check + Overlap guard).
- GET /my-leaves: User history.
- PUT /:id/cancel: Withdraw pending requests.
- GET /balance: Real-time day counters.
- GET /all: (Admin) Global overview.
- PUT /:id/status: (Admin) Approval/Rejection workflow.
- GET /statistics: (Admin) High-level system metrics.

USER & ADMIN MANAGEMENT (/api/users)
- POST /request-admin: Initiates 7-day cooldown logic.
- GET /admin-requests: (Admin) Pending role elevations.
- PUT /:id/handle-admin-request: (Admin) Promote/Demote logic.
- PUT /:id/leave-balance: (Admin) Manual balance overrides.

================================================================================
5. SECURITY & BUSINESS RULES
================================================================================
1. RBAC: Multi-layered middleware ensures User vs Admin separation.
2. Stateless Auth: JWTs are used for all protected interactions, avoiding 
   server-side session overhead.
3. Data Integrity: All dates are handled as UTC objects to prevent time-zone 
   shifts in leave reporting.
4. Acquiescence: Leaves are automatically accrued/reset via server-side 
   cron jobs.

================================================================================
6. PROJECT ROADMAP & SETUP
================================================================================
1. Installation: Run 'npm install' in both client/ and server/ root.
2. Environment: Ensure .env contains MONGO_URI, JWT_SECRET, and CLIENT_URL.
3. Execution:
    - Backend: npm start (or npm run dev)
    - Frontend: npm run dev
